 "standard_text": "Change between index and logarithm form; use the laws of logarithms; use given logarithms to find others; solve simple logarithmic equations. (summary of the NERDC SSS 1 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free SSS 1 maths worksheets on logarithms: index and log form, laws of logarithms, using log 2 and log 3, and solving logarithmic equations. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "log_b N = n means bⁿ = N",
 "key_sub": "log ab = log a + log b",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>A logarithm is a power: log₂ 8 = 3 because 2³ = 8.</li><li>log ab = log a + log b, log (a ÷ b) = log a − log b, log aⁿ = n log a.</li><li>log 10 = 1 and log 1 = 0 in base ten.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>log 4 + log 25</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>log 100</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 2</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Solve log₃ x = 4</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x = 3⁴</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 81</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>log (a + b) = log a + log b</td><td>That is false. The law is for a product.</td></tr><tr><td>Dividing logs: log a ÷ log b</td><td>log a − log b is log (a ÷ b).</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting the base</td><td>log with no base means base ten.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
